From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruskin Constant <ruskin@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:28:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Map smooth and high-quality image-rendering to high paint
 quality

stylo's ImageRendering gains Smooth (un-gated) and HighQuality (new)
variants for the servo build; this match was exhaustive over the old
three-variant servo enum and needs the two new arms to compile. Both
map to peniko's High quality, since the spec defines them as
behaviorally identical, higher-quality alternatives to the Medium
default.
---
 src/render.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/render.rs b/src/render.rs
index 50a9a6e..293dfe6 100644
--- a/src/render.rs
+++ b/src/render.rs
@@ -751,6 +751,9 @@ impl<'dom, 'a> BlitzDomPainter<'dom, 'a> {
 fn to_image_quality(image_rendering: ImageRendering) -> peniko::ImageQuality {
     match image_rendering {
         ImageRendering::Auto => peniko::ImageQuality::Medium,
+        // smooth and high-quality are spec-defined to behave identically
+        // (both request the best available sampling).
+        ImageRendering::Smooth | ImageRendering::HighQuality => peniko::ImageQuality::High,
         ImageRendering::CrispEdges => peniko::ImageQuality::Low,
         ImageRendering::Pixelated => peniko::ImageQuality::Low,
     }
